// Title: Suspicious CustomShellHost Execution
// Sigma ID: 84b14121-9d14-416e-800b-f3b829c5a14d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-19 | Modified: 2025-10-29
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1216
// Description: Detects the execution of CustomShellHost.exe where the child isn't located in
//   'C:\Windows\explorer.exe'. CustomShellHost is a known LOLBin that can be abused by attackers for
//   defense evasion techniques.
// False positives:
//   - False positives are unlikely, investigate matches carefully.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/pull/180
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/CustomShellHost/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_customshellhost_susp_exec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\CustomShellHost.exe" and (not(FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe"))
